    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d54">

                <pb facs="0143" n="121" sameAs="frus:frus1950v05/pg121"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">886A.2553/12–3150: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hare</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-12-31T12:00:00+03:00">December 31,
                            1950—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>417. From Brewer. Aramco–SAG negotiations concluded late last night December
                    30th, with agreement signed between Finance Minister and Davies in which profit
                    sharing principle put forward by company accepted by SAG and outstanding SAG
                    demands officially withdrawn. Company officials appear pleased with results,
                    which they terming “the December 1950 agreement”, stating that they gave in to
                    SAG on a few minor points only to obtain agreement. Entire Aramco party,
                    including Owen, left by plane for Luxor this morning, making it impossible
                    obtain details agreement, but George Hay and Bob Brougham proceeding directly
                    Cairo and New York with signed original. New York and Washington offices should
                    have copies by January 3–4 and have been asked communicate details Department
                        soonest.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d54-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>For [Parker?]: Brougham hopes be in Cairo New Year’s Day and to see you.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 417; repeated information Dhahran 214, Cairo 91. [Brewer.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hare</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d54-f1" n="1" xml:id="d54-f1-content">
                <p>Further documentation on the agreement is scheduled for publication in a
                    forthcoming volume of <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>.</p>
            </note>
